sec.p:
Calculation of contour length and persistence length of DNA origami monomers from AFM images were done by custom scripts using MATLAB R2017b software (MathWorks Inc.). Refer to the previous report for a more detailed procedure (31). Briefly, collected individual monomer structures were converted into binary images to be thinned and skeletonized to obtain their contours. A parametric spline was used to fit the contour of each individual structure. The persistence length was measured with characteristic points of the fitting spline from every well-folded structure using a modified version of the open-source software tool Easyworm (33). Using the WLC model, the mean-square end-to-end distance (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
